<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gardman</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gardman was a district of Caucasian Albania in the hills west of the Kura river, in present-day western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a>. In the late 6th century it became the domain of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mihranid-dynasty">Mihranids</a>, a branch of a great Parthian noble family, who made it the base from which they ruled Albania as princes in the 7th and 8th centuries. Its stronghold is mentioned in the History of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albanians">Albanians</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gardman.jpg" alt="Gardman" width="320" height="265" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: www.armenica.org · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jorgat_harasm.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
